Third-party data redistributed in this repository
-------------------------------------------------

1. data/external/lm_sentiment_words.csv
   Derived from the Loughran-McDonald Master Dictionary (1993-2025 release),
   Software Repository for Accounting and Finance, University of Notre Dame.
   https://sraf.nd.edu/loughranmcdonald-master-dictionary/
   The dictionary and its sentiment word lists are free for use in academic
   research; commercial use requires a licence from the authors
   (loughranmcdonald@gmail.com). Only the word-to-category mapping for the
   seven categories used here is redistributed, not the full master file.
   Cite: Loughran, T., & McDonald, B. (2011), Journal of Finance 66(1), 35-65.

2. data/external/underwriter_ranks.csv
   Derived from "Underwriter-Rank.xls" published by Jay R. Ritter, University
   of Florida. https://site.warrington.ufl.edu/ritter/ipo-data/
   Reshaped to one row per underwriter and listing year; the underlying
   Carter-Manaster scores are unchanged.
   Cite: Carter, R. B., & Manaster, S. (1990), Journal of Finance 45(4),
   1045-1067, with rankings updated by Loughran & Ritter (2004) and Ritter.

3. data/external/company_sic_codes.csv and data/raw/market_indices.csv
   SIC codes are US government works from the SEC's company submissions API
   and are not subject to copyright. Market index closes are factual daily
   observations retrieved from Yahoo Finance.

Data NOT redistributed
----------------------

The stockanalysis.com IPO calendar is not committed. Their terms permit
snippets with attribution but not republishing content in full, and the raw
scrape is close to a verbatim copy of their tables. Regenerate it with
src/scraper_ipo_calendar.py. The derived analysis dataset in data/processed/
is a transformed research dataset joined against SEC and Yahoo Finance
sources, not a copy of their table.

SEC EDGAR filing text is a US government-hosted public disclosure and is not
committed here only because of its size; src/scraper_edgar.py retrieves it.
